The driver workaround database contained ~25 entries for hardware from 1999–2010 that no longer exists in any realistic deployment, and two feature wrapper functions had correctness issues.

## Removed: obsolete EMBEDDED_OVERRIDES entries
All entries were for pre-2010 hardware: Intel GMA 950/3150/Solano, ATI Radeon 7xxx/9xxx, 3Dlabs, Trident, Matrox G400, ELSA TNT2 Vanta, Sun Expert3D, Mesa 6.x/7.x. The `DriverInfo`/`FeatureOverride` structs, `matchesPattern`/`matchesDriver`/`findOverride` helpers, and `isBroken`/`isDisabled` now return `FALSE` unconditionally.

Additionally, all `SLOW`-status entries were dead code — the public API only calls `isBroken`/`isDisabled`; no `isSlow()` path exists.

## Fixed: `multidraw_elements_wrapper`
Was doing a raw extension string lookup instead of using the proper glue function:
```cpp
// before
return SoGLContext_glext_supported(glue, "GL_EXT_multi_draw_arrays");
// after
return SoGLContext_has_multidraw_vertex_arrays(glue);
```

## Fixed: `glsl_clip_vertex_hw_wrapper`
Removed blanket ATI vendor exclusion based on a 2007 AMD driver paper. Modern AMD drivers have supported hardware clip vertex for years:
```cpp
// before
if (!SoGLContext_has_arb_vertex_shader(glue)) return FALSE;
if (glue->vendor_is_ati) return FALSE;
return TRUE;
// after
return SoGLContext_has_arb_vertex_shader(glue);
```

