## Summary

Closes #17. Supersedes PR #14 (fixes its backwards-compatibility break).

## Problem

Custom event classes registered via `dispatchesEvents` only received the owning model — no relation name, pivot IDs, or pivot attributes. PR #14 attempted to fix this but unconditionally passed a second `$payload` argument, causing `ArgumentCountError` for any existing event class with a single-argument constructor.

## Solution

A new **opt-in interface** gates payload delivery:

```php
// src/Contracts/ReceivesPivotPayload.php
namespace GeneaLabs\LaravelPivotEvents\Contracts;

interface ReceivesPivotPayload
{
    public function __construct(Model $model, array $payload);
}
```

- Classes that **implement** `ReceivesPivotPayload` → instantiated as `new EventClass($model, $payload)`
- Classes that **don't** → instantiated as `new EventClass($model)` ← unchanged, zero breaking change

Detection uses `is_a($eventClass, ReceivesPivotPayload::class, true)` — no reflection, no string parsing.

## Payload shape

Matches what the generic `eloquent.*` listeners already receive:

| Key | Type | Description |
|-----|------|-------------|
| `model` | `Model` | The owning model instance |
| `relation` | `string` | Relation method name (e.g. `'roles'`) |
| `pivotIds` | `array` | Affected pivot IDs |
| `pivotIdsAttributes` | `array` | Pivot column values keyed by ID |

## Usage

```php
use GeneaLabs\LaravelPivotEvents\Contracts\ReceivesPivotPayload;
use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Model;

class UserRoleAttached implements ReceivesPivotPayload
{
    public function __construct(Model $model, array $payload)
    {
        // $payload['relation']           => 'roles'
        // $payload['pivotIds']           => [1, 2]
        // $payload['pivotIdsAttributes'] => [1 => ['value' => 42], ...]
    }
}

// In the model:
protected $dispatchesEvents = [
    'pivotAttached' => UserRoleAttached::class,
];
```

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Existing event class with `__construct(Model $model)` continues to work — no `ArgumentCountError`
- [x] New event class implementing `ReceivesPivotPayload` receives `model`, `relation`, `pivotIds`, `pivotIdsAttributes`
- [x] All 35 existing tests still pass
- [x] 3 new dedicated tests in `tests/DispatchesEventsTest.php`

